.TH FILE-ORGANIZER 1 "October 2026" "file-organizer 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
file-organizer \- organize files into category folders
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B file-organizer
.RI [ COMMAND ] " [options]"
.br
.B file-organizer gui
.RI [ \-\-toolkit " auto|qt|tk" ]
.br
.B file-organizer scan
.I DIRECTORY
.RI [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B file-organizer organize
.I DIRECTORY
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B file-organizer undo
.RI [ \-\-yes ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
File Organizer sorts files into category folders (Images, Documents, Audio, …)
with a live preview, undo support, and a scriptable command-line interface.
Running it without arguments (or via the desktop launcher) opens the graphical
interface. Moves never silently overwrite existing files: clashes are renamed
.RI ( image.jpg " \(-> " image\ (1).jpg )
by default.
.SH ORGANIZE OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-only " Categories"
Comma-separated subset of categories (default: all).
.TP
.BR \-\-include\-other
Also file uncategorized items into an
.IR Other /
folder.
.TP
.BR \-\-recursive
Descend into subdirectories (destination and hidden folders excluded).
.TP
.BR \-\-conflict " rename|skip|overwrite"
What to do when the destination exists (default:
.BR rename ).
.B overwrite
replaces files and asks for confirmation in the GUI.
.TP
.BR \-\-delete\-empty
Remove empty folders afterwards (hidden folders and symlinks are never removed).
.TP
.BR \-\-dry\-run
Print the move plan without moving anything.
.TP
.BR \-\-yes
Skip the confirmation prompt (for scripts).
.SH EXAMPLES
Show what would happen, moving nothing:
.PP
.RS
file-organizer organize ~/Downloads --dry-run
.RE
.PP
Organize only images and documents, renaming on conflict:
.PP
.RS
file-organizer organize ~/Downloads --only Images,Documents
.RE
.PP
Reverse the last run:
.PP
.RS
file-organizer undo
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/file-organizer/settings.json
Categories and preferences.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/file-organizer/last-run.json
Undo log of the most recent organize run.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR python3 (1)
